1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,527
For decades, scientists called Easter Island a cautionary tale.

2
00:00:04,477 --> 00:00:08,500
A civilization that collapsed because it destroyed its own environment.

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:10,215
But there's a problem.

4
00:00:10,215 --> 00:00:14,295
The Rapa Nui survived for centuries after the forests were gone.

5
00:00:14,295 --> 00:00:17,136
Their oral history tells a different story.

6
00:00:17,136 --> 00:00:18,738
Ships came.

7
00:00:18,738 --> 00:00:20,818
Then people disappeared.

8
00:00:20,818 --> 00:00:26,568
In 1863, Peruvian slave ships seized fourteen hundred people in a single raid.

9
00:00:26,568 --> 00:00:29,170
Smallpox killed the survivors.

10
00:00:29,170 --> 00:00:32,874
The population fell from three thousand to one hundred eleven.

11
00:00:32,874 --> 00:00:34,806
In less than a decade.

12
00:00:34,806 --> 00:00:38,181
We spent a century blaming them for their own extinction.

13
00:00:38,181 --> 00:00:40,431
The real cause had a name.

14
00:00:40,431 --> 00:00:41,943
It was us.

